{
  "_comment": "Employer career sites read directly (no agencies). Each entry: name (as it should appear), ats, id (board name from the careers URL), country (home country, ISO-2), optional register_name (legal name on the UK sponsor register if different, so the licence check matches). Workday also needs host + site from https://<host>/<site>. Set \"local\": true when every vacancy is in the home country (e.g. an NHS trust or university), \"enabled\": false to pause one. Board ids below are a starter set and should be checked after the first run: any that fail are listed on the board under Data sources. Find an employer's id by opening its careers page and looking at the job links.",
  "_how_to_find": {
    "greenhouse": "boards.greenhouse.io/<id> or job-boards.greenhouse.io/<id>",
    "lever": "jobs.lever.co/<id>  (jobs.eu.lever.co/<id> -> add \"region\": \"eu\")",
    "ashby": "jobs.ashbyhq.com/<id>",
    "smartrecruiters": "jobs.smartrecruiters.com/<id>",
    "workable": "apply.workable.com/<id>",
    "recruitee": "<id>.recruitee.com",
    "personio": "<id>.jobs.personio.de  (or .com -> add \"tld\": \"com\")",
    "workday": "<host>/<site>, e.g. gsk.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/GSKCareers -> host gsk.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com, site GSKCareers",
    "oracle": "<host>/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/<site>, e.g. encd.fa.em3.oraclecloud.com ... sites/CX_3001 -> host + site",
    "successfactors": "career sites whose images load from rmkcdn.successfactors.com: host is the careers domain (jobs.swissport.com); optional keywords list for very large sites"
  },
